            <ArticleTitle>Management of a heavily exuding, painful wound with necrotising subcutaneous infection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>25-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Wounds with necrotising fasciitis are often malodorous and produce copious exudate. Selecting appropriate dressings can alleviate these symptoms and improve the patient's quality of life within a short time period.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
